@startuml descriptor-mission-skill-glossary
' Sources:
'   src/charter/offering/missions/step_contracts.py   (MissionStepContract; no JSON schema file)
'   src/charter/offering/schemas/skill.schema.yaml + pack_skills/models.py (PackSkill)
'   ADR-0049 (GlossaryContext, Term); today's glossary_packs/models.py (GlossaryPack) is superseded
' Notation: + required, - optional (Pydantic default shown after =).
' Decided design: ADR-0049 (glossary contexts and terms) and ADR-0050 (step contract moves into the mission-type
' bundle, loses gates), accepted 2026-11-02; not built yet. PackSkill is unchanged.
' Pending: a yellow <<pending>> class or a [pending ADR-00xx OQn] suffix marks a part whose open question is not ruled.
!include _style.iuml
title Mission-step contract, pack skill and glossary descriptor schemas — decided design (ADR-0049, ADR-0050)

class MissionStepContract <<step_contracts.py>> {
  + id : string
  + schema_version : string
  + action : string
  + mission : string
  + steps : ContractStep[1..]
}
note right of MissionStepContract
  Kept as a kind (ADR-0050 d5). File moves into the bundle:
  mission_types/<type>/step_contracts/<id>.step-contract.yaml (d4);
  today's suffix is kept if it differs (d5).
  gates and GateBinding are removed (follow-ups); a binding migrates
  to a guard on a lifecycle transition (ADR-0050 d12).
end note
class ContractStep {
  + id : string
  + description : string
  - command : string
  - inputs : StepInput[] = []
  - delegates_to : DelegatesTo
  - guidance : string
}
class StepInput {
  + flag : string
  + source : string
  - optional : bool = false
}
class DelegatesTo {
  + kind : ArtifactKind
  + candidates : string[1..]
}
MissionStepContract *-- "1..*" ContractStep
ContractStep *-- "*" StepInput
ContractStep *-- "0..1" DelegatesTo

class PackSkill <<skill.schema.yaml>> {
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + id : string [<=64] ~ id pattern (see note)
  + title : string
  + description : string
  + form : prompt | wrapper
  - body_path : string [required iff form=prompt]
  - expands_to : SkillExpansion [required iff form=wrapper]
  - triggers : string[] = []
  - parameters : SkillParameter[] = []
  - invocation : SkillInvocation
  - tools : string[] = ["*"]
  - version : string = "1.0.0"
  - maintainers : string[]
  - overrides : string
  - enhances : string
}
class SkillExpansion {
  + target : string ~ builtin:... | cli:spec-kitty ...
  - args : string
}
class SkillParameter {
  + name : string
  - required : bool = false
  - description : string
  - default : string
}
class SkillInvocation {
  - user_invocable : bool = true
  - model_invocable : bool = true
  - side_effects : string[]
}
PackSkill *-- "0..1" SkillExpansion
PackSkill *-- "*" SkillParameter
PackSkill *-- "0..1" SkillInvocation

class GlossaryContext <<glossary.schema.json (ADR-0049 d1, d2)>> {
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + id : string (kebab-case, the file stem)
  + name : string
  + description : string (its applicability)
  - tags : string[1..]
  - applies_to : AppliesTo <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0049 OQ2: advisory]</color>
  + terms : Term[1..]
  --
  file: glossaries/<context-id>.glossary.yaml <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0049 OQ1]</color>
  URN glossary:<id> <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0049 OQ3]</color>
}
class AppliesTo {
  - paths : string[] (globs)
  - languages : string[]
  - stacks : string[] (once #163 lands)
}
class Term <<an item inside a context, not an artifact (d3)>> {
  + id : string (kebab-case, unique in the context)
  + name : string (canonical surface form)
  + definition : string
  - examples : string[]
  - aliases : string[]
  - avoid : string[]
  + status : TermStatus <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0049 OQ4]</color>
  - see_also : string[] (term URNs)
  --
  URN term:<context-id>/<term-id> (d4)
}
enum TermStatus <<pending>> {
  draft
  active
  deprecated
}
GlossaryContext *-- "1..*" Term
GlossaryContext *-- "0..1" AppliesTo
Term --> TermStatus
Term ..> Term : see_also
note bottom of Term
  Dropped (d5): confidence, introduced_in_mission, provenance.
  surface becomes name; synonyms_to_avoid becomes avoid;
  banned_synonyms folds into avoid.
  Only a clash on the same term: URN is a conflict (d12, d13).
end note
note right of PackSkill
  id pattern (skill.schema.yaml:21):
  ""^(?!.*<U+005C>n)[a-z][a-z0-9]*(-[a-z0-9]+)*$""
end note
legend right
  + required, - optional.
  Yellow <<pending>> / [pending …]: decided in the cited ADR,
  but the cited open question is not ruled.
endlegend
@enduml
